{
  "id": "29449_meikoku",
  "headword": "銘刻",
  "reading": "めいこく",
  "romaji": "meikoku",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "inscription; engraving",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "inscription; engraving; engraved characters",
      "explanation": "Letters or designs carved into metal, stone, or other hard material, or the act of carving them. Also used figuratively for something engraved deeply in the heart or memory."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29449_meikoku_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦{石碑|せきひ}→石碑：13725_sekihi⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{銘刻|めいこく}する。",
      "english": "to inscribe a stone monument.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29449_meikoku_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{古|ふる}い→古い：00488_furui⟧⟦{鐘|かね}→鐘：02654_kane⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{銘刻|めいこく}された⟦{文字|もじ}→文字：03632_moji⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{読|よ}む→読む：00426_yomu⟧。",
      "english": "to read the characters engraved on an old bell.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29449_meikoku_ex3",
      "japanese": "⟦その→その：00993_sono⟧⟦{言葉|ことば}→言葉：02880_kotoba⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧⟦{今|いま}→今：00945_ima⟧⟦も→も：00484_mo⟧⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{銘刻|めいこく}されて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧。",
      "english": "Those words are engraved in my heart even now.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal word used both literally for carved inscriptions and figuratively for vivid, lasting impressions.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{石|いし}→石：02177_ishi⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{銘刻|めいこく}する: to engrave in stone\n- ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{銘刻|めいこく}する: to engrave in one's heart\n- {銘刻|めいこく}された⟦{文字|もじ}→文字：03632_moji⟧: engraved characters\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{刻印|こくいん}→刻印：29469_kokuin⟧: stamp; engraved mark — emphasizes a stamped or imprinted mark\n- ⟦{銘記|めいき}→銘記：17488_meiki⟧: to bear firmly in mind — figurative only, never a physical carving",
